{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.TopologicalMassEigenspaceDecomp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.TopologicalMassEigenspaceDecomp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.JetProlongation"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_eigenspace_transientPart_isTransient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_eigenspace_transientPart_isTransient","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-eigenspace-decomp.lean#L70-L82","doc":"The transient part of `x` lies in the transient subalgebra\n`𝒜_{n+1}^{trans} = ker τ̂ₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_eigenspace_descendedPart_isDescended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_eigenspace_descendedPart_isDescended","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-eigenspace-decomp.lean#L56-L68","doc":"The descended part of `x` lies in the descended subalgebra\n`𝒜_{n+1}^{desc} = im τ̂ₙ = im ℓₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_eigenspace_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_eigenspace_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-eigenspace-decomp.lean#L35-L54","doc":"**Eigenspace decomposition under the descent involution.**\n\nFor any `JetChain` with carriers `EndAlg n`, every element `x ∈\nEndAlg (n+1)` decomposes as the sum of its descended part\n(image of `τ̂ₙ`) and its transient part (kernel of `τ̂ₙ`).  This\nis the structural statement that powers the Killing-form\northogonality + multiplicative-integral additivity used in the\nmass-identity proof. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:topological-mass-eigenspace-decomp","label":"lem:topological-mass-eigenspace-decomp","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-eigenspace-decomp.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}